# Generated native projects (expo prebuild). Kept out of git so the app builds
# from app.json + the config plugins as the single source of truth — the same
# model foodyzzhq uses. While these were tracked, every prebuild rewrote them
# with fresh object UUIDs and dirtied the tree, and the version had to be
# hand-propagated into build.gradle / Info.plist or EAS would ship the old one.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash ON PURPOSE: a bare `android/` or `ios/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which would also swallow the shipped
# assets below. Anchoring means they can never be caught in the first place.
#
#   assets/sounds/android      assets/sounds/IOS
#   assets/customer/android    assets/customer/ios
#   assets/images/logo/android assets/images/logo/ios
#
# EAS respects .gitignore (it resolves paths with `git check-ignore --no-index`),
# so an over-broad rule here silently ships an app with no notification sounds
# or icons. Verify with `git check-ignore --no-index -v <path>` after any edit.
/android/
/ios/
